Chapter: PunctualLaunderBuiltin

 Probe (closed by the punctual FIX campaign): the safe-builtin
 allowlist is tightened to genuinely constant-time, allocation-free
 builtins. show (and integer-to-text, text-starts-with, text-compare)
 are off the list - show allocates a fresh Text inside the "no heap"
 discipline - so the call draws CDX6001. The original probe also
 accused list-length, but the emitter refutes that: runtime lists
 are length-prefixed contiguous vectors and list-length is a single
 header load, so it STAYS allowlisted and the second operand here is
 the legal half of the probe.

Section: Definitions

  punctual spend : Integer, List Integer -> Integer
  spend (x) (xs) = text-length (show x) + list-length xs

  opening : Text = show (spend 12345 [1, 2, 3])

